{
  "note": [
    "Radiation Lock West's fabric, cut from the one Lawanda layout in scripts/fabric-lawanda.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. 4.0 x 3.6 x 4.8 about the eye: the western half of the bare decontamination chamber, Floyd's squash court -- no showers, nozzles or panels. Its package's own light (lighting.fixtures) is the room's.",
    "THE CHAMBER RUNS DUE EAST, NOT ALONG THE MAIN LAB'S BEARING 45 as RADIATION-LOCK-WEST's beyond texts measure it: on that bearing it would run into Physical Plant Two, and the Radiation Lab could not share its south wall with the Bio Lab. So its west end is RAKED onto the Main Lab's NE chamfer, 45 degrees across the chamber, parallel to the chamfer and 2T from it, and the door (2.4 x 3.0, RAD-DOOR-WEST, drawn shut while it lacks OPENBIT) sits on the chamfer's normal through the Main Lab's door -- 0.353 m NORTH of this chamber's axis, because the chamber's north wall stands 2T inside the plant's south wall. The north wall is 6.05 m long and the south wall 1.25 m.",
    "West through the door when open: the Main Lab, looked into on a bearing about 45 degrees round from square -- its floor, and across it the SW branch and the west mouth. East: no wall; the chamber runs straight on through Radiation Lock East to RAD-DOOR-EAST 6.0 m from the eye, the warning plate north of it (lettered by the painting), and through that door when open the Radiation Lab's blue."
  ],
